# Harness Wiring Conventions

## Reconcile every wiring document, not just the one you changed

**Read `docs/RECONCILIATION-RULES.md` Rule 1 before finalizing any wiring change.** A change
to one wiring document is not done until it has been checked against the source-of-truth
chain **and** every other wiring surface listed there — including the ones you did not edit.
They must all agree.

## Source of truth

`XTREMEX-IO-TABLE.html` is the living pin source of truth. `SCHEMATIC-WIRING.html`, the
interactive schematic app, and the three `.harness` files are **faces** of it, not peers. New
pin facts go into the table first, then propagate. The harness.design app copy is a mirror —
pull from the repo into it, never treat it as the source.

Dated `VERIFY` / `AUDIT` / `FACES` / `BOARD-VERIFY` notes in `docs/` are frozen records. Read
them; never update them; never treat them as living pin maps.

## Which file a wire belongs in

**Every ECU pin is Signal by default.** Two carve-outs go to Power: the ECU 12V ignition
supply with its power-hold wiring, and **all relay trigger outputs** (so each relay circuit
stays whole in one drawing).

- **All** pedal (APS) pins are Signal — supplies included. (This reverses an earlier rule
  that put pins 1/2/4/5 in Power.)
- **All** ETB pins are Signal — motor pair included.
- **All** 5V sensor power is Signal, including the 5V splices.
- Only 12V circuits not named above are Power.

A part legitimately appears in both files when it has both a power pin and a signal pin
(injectors, COPs, the MRS control connector). That is not duplication.

## Bulkheads

**There are exactly two bulkhead connectors, A and B, and they are HDP20 from owned stock:**

- Loom A: `HDP24-24-47PE-L017` firewall to `HDP26-24-47SE-L015` engine plug (47 cavities)
- Loom B: `HDP24-24-21PN` firewall to `HDP26-24-21SN` engine plug (21 cavities)

Bulkhead C is deleted. The earlier Souriau 8STA 37-way design is **superseded** — do not
reintroduce it. Bulkheads are real connectors, not OEM blocks.

Every wire crossing the firewall terminates in a bulkhead cavity: two wires (`<id>_c` cabin
side, `<id>_e` engine side), not one wire passing through.

Pin priority: **every shield gets its own bulkhead pin first**, then sensor 5V and ground are
spliced at the bulkhead connector.

## Harness C — Engine Room Harness

Separate loom, **no bulkhead connector**. Exits the driver fender and runs around the front of
the engine bay. Carries radiator fan, condenser fan, EPS pump, headlights and headlight
motors, turn, horn, wipers, washer pump. Nothing else comes off A/B except the EPS pump. All
IAT sensors stay in the engine harness.

## Drawing conventions

- OEM body/engine-bay connections (relays, clutch, cruise stalk, brake, reverse, start,
  ignition switch, AC amplifier) are generic **blocks** — draw only the wires this harness
  lands; do not invent OEM internal pinouts.
- Real pinouts only for parts this build controls: Link Superseal A/B/comms, aftermarket
  sensors we specify, and the BRZ e-throttle pedal (6-pin Sumitomo TS 025 — not a 4-pin APS).
- Ignition Switch is a dummy OEM block feeding **DI 9 (B28)** for ECU Hold Power (PCLink
  Ignition Switch function, paired with the Aux 6 relay hold).
- No wire runs direct to a device — every device gets a connector.
- Shields: terminated at the ECU end only, floating at the device end. Model a shielded run as
  a **cable** whose `shield` core has a `source` and **no `target`**. Device-end connectors
  carry no shell.
- Layout stays orthogonal on a 30px grid.

Full build rules: `docs/HARNESS-CONSOLIDATION-AND-LAYOUT-PLAN.md` §6.
